                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30 active" data-rel="tab-a-1">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">How do I decide which programme to choose, or which programme is right
                                for me?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer active" id="tab-a-1">If you are dealing with complex family dynamics or need
                            long-term business transformation, leadership growth, and legacy building, OPM is the right
                            choice. It is a 12-month programme for those focused on sustainable growth, succession, and
                            global business exposure.
                            <br> <br>
                            If there are not too many complications in your family dynamics, your primary pain point is
                            sales or business acceleration, and you want to make a shorter commitment of your time, then
                            9-month BAP is a better program for you.

                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-2">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> What is the main outcome difference?
                            </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <div class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-a-2">

                            <div class="detailsList faq-log">
                                <ul class="list">
                                    <li>
                                        <p>
                                            12 months OPM = holistic, sustainable transformation and leadership
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <p>
                                            9 months BAP = fast, practical sales and process gains
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-3">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> Will there be the same level of rigour of practical application in
                                both the programs?
                            </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-3">Yes. Both programs include assignments and Capstone to ensure
                            whatever is taught in the class is thoroughly applied in your company. A pressing problem
                            that your organisation is currently facing is solved with the help of Capstone, with one on
                            one coaching by faculty and mentors.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-4">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Will I miss out a lot by choosing the BAP?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-4">It's all about what your need is. Yes, you will miss out on
                            some aspects like in-depth modules for family, self, patriarch, non family CXOs. Also,
                            international immersions and Fractional Board. Nevertheless, if your current pressing need
                            is revenue growth, then you can go for BAP.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-5">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> Is it worth doing the 12-month program if my goal is only sales
                                growth?
                            </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-5">It is better to compare all aspects of both programs, what
                            different and additional you are getting in each, and then decide.
                        </p>
                    </div>

