                <div id="tab55" class="content">

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-e-1">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Is the business simulation/ personal interview conducted online or
                                offline?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-e-1">The in-person business simulation and
                            interview will be conducted on the same day for a student. These will be scheduled across
                            major cities (Delhi, Bengaluru, Mumbai, Ahmedabad, Indore, Hyderabad, Chandigarh) in India
                            and over Zoom in exceptional cases.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-e-2">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What is GD or business simulation ? How to prepare for it?
                            </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-e-2">The in-person business simulation will
                            require students to role-play as a CXO of a company and solve its business challenges in a
                            team of 5-6 applicants. We will send them a case study to prepare for the business
                            simulation round 3-4 days prior for preparation. In this round, they will be judged on their
                            creativity, communication, and teamwork skills. They will be participating in a group
                            discussion for 45 minutes followed by a presentation (without any slides).</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-e-3">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What happens in the personal interview, what kind of questions will be
                                asked?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-e-3">The interview will be a one-on-one
                            conversation with our faculty or senior leadership. The questions will be around their
                            application and motivations for applying to Masters' Union. The goal is to know more about
                            students and what they want to achieve at Masters' Union.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-e-4">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Is there any detailed information about GD/PI ?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>

                        <div class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-e-4">

                            <div class="detailsList faq-log">
                                <ul class="list">
                                    <li>
                                        <p>
                                            The overall process will take around 3 hours.

                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <p>
                                            The business simulation will last 45 minutes followed by a 15 minute group
                                            presentation. Students will be working in teams of 4-6 students on a
                                            simulated
                                            business scenario, where students will be expected to make decisions,
                                            analyse
                                            data and present their findings.


                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <p>The interview will be conducted by a senior leader or a faculty member at
                                            Masters’ Union and will be approximately 30 minutes long. They will be asked
                                            questions about their application including their achievements, essays and
                                            the
                                            video essay submitted.</p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <p> Dress code for the event is smart casuals.</p>
                                    </li>

                                </ul>

                            </div>
                        </div>



